{
  "_about": "Manual ground-truth labels for the 2026Q2 hot-spots dataset. Each hotspot was reviewed against Esri World Imagery (~1-3 year vintage in PH) by comparing a 240m-wide tile centered on the hotspot's lat/lon. Labels: 'solar' if a visible panel-grid array was clearly identifiable on a rooftop; 'not_solar' if no panels were visible despite the rooftop having clearly changed; 'unclear' if the imagery was ambiguous (could be panels, could be material change, could be cloudy/old); 'missing' if Esri returned 500 for that lat/lon (mostly rural areas outside hi-res coverage).",
  "_methodology": "Reviewer: Claude (sonnet-vision), 2026-05-08. Single-pass, no second-reviewer adjudication. Calibration: A solar array is visible at this resolution as dark blue/black rectangular gridded patches on rooftops, typically 5-50m on a side. Reroofing or fresh asphalt darkens but lacks the regular grid structure. Greenhouses appear as light-colored long structures and were marked not_solar.",
  "_caveats": [
    "Esri World Imagery in the Philippines is typically 1-3 years old. Solar installs from 2024-2026 may not yet be visible. Real precision is therefore likely HIGHER than the published number; this is a lower bound.",
    "12 of 181 hotspots have no usable imagery (Esri 500 for remote rural areas). The reviewable population is 169.",
    "Single-reviewer labeling has inter-rater bias. A second reviewer would tighten the unclear category.",
    "The hotspot extraction uses NIR-only local-anomaly, not the multi-channel NIR+SWIR fingerprint. A v1.1 extraction tightened to multi-channel would likely have higher precision."
  ],
  "_aggregate": {
    "total_attempted": 181,
    "missing_imagery": 12,
    "reviewable": 169,
    "solar": 6,
    "unclear": 16,
    "not_solar": 147,
    "precision_strict_unclear_as_not_solar": 0.0355,
    "precision_lenient_unclear_as_solar": 0.1302,
    "interpretation": "At current hot-spot extraction sensitivity, fewer than 1 in 5 hotspots show visible panels even under the most generous interpretation. The signal exists at city-aggregate scale but is too noisy for confident per-pin claims."
  },
